If you also think it's slimy to use what the game gives you, don't read 
this.




If you have a pet which is interested in gold, give them some to carry 
around.  Every time they pick something up and then drop it, they will
leave behind as much gold as they were carrying, up to around 10,000 gp.
But they will still be carrying as much gold as they were originally.
If you pick that gold up and give it to your pet, they will then have
about twice as much gold as they did before.  

The reason I say about is that they actually drop a random amount of gold, 
although it is always pretty close to what they're carrying.  (Unless you 
were foolish enough to give them more than 10,000 gold pieces.)
It seems like this randomness must be part of the original design, even
if the pet business isn't, because it's hard to imagine how such a bug
could come about by accident.  My guess is that the designers wanted
you to have a way to generate gold, just not such an efficient way.

The way it works, if you ignore the pet bug but still want to make some
cash, is you can get more money by giving money to some monster that 
picks up gold, and then killing him.  As nethack works currently, the 
monster will give you back your gold, plus interest.  Thus, if you ran 
into the mother of all throne rooms, with a hundred orcs in it, you could 
drop 1000 gold pieces on the door step, lure them to the gold, and then 
bop them.  When the next orc picked up the gold, there'd be that much 
more of it for him, and the interest could keep compounding as you waited 
and killed.

If this randomness were kept but the pet trick were removed, then giving
money to orcs, etc., works almost like the bank in Larn.  In Larn, if you
have some extra gold sitting around not doing you any good, you deposit
it in the bank, and it earns interest for you.  In Nethack, the orcs give
you the interest.  And in both cases, there is a maximum deposit.

I'm not sure if I ever checked, but it would be cool if, when you dropped
your gold in one of Croesus' vaults, the gold collected interest.  If it
doesn't now, maybe the dev team would consider making it so?

Well, those are my thoughts on the how and the why of the gold generation
bugs.

